Texto:
{*1[Passive]}
With your incredible drawpower, each arrow you fire can penetrate even the thickest armor or carapace.

Also increases the size of your quiver.

{*1[Passive]}
By affixing small barbs to your arrows, each Longbow shot has a chance to deal heavy Bleeding Damage to your foes.

Also increases the size of your quiver.

{*1[Weapon Attacks]}
Your skill with Longbows enables you to fire multiple arrows simultaneously.

Also increases the size of your quiver.

{*1[Active - Sustained]}
The razor sharp blades of your weapons cut into your foes with ease.
While this Ability is active, Critical Hit Damage for Longswords, Daggers, Faeblades, and Greatswords is substantially increased.

{*1[Weapon Attacks]}
Your skill with the Longbow allows you to fire a volley of arrows into the sky, raining death down on your foes.

Also increases the size of your quiver.

{*1[Passive]}
Your deadly grace allows you to deal tremendous amounts of damage from stealth.

Unlocks new sneak attacks with Daggers or Faeblades that can instantly kill an unaware enemy if you deal enough damage.

{LINE_CENTER} This small journal, apparently written by a man named Jared, is soaked with blood on the inside from it's owners wounds or perhaps other sources. Most pages are unreadable for the most part.
{LINE_SPACE}
{LINE_CENTER} As you flip through the final few pages however, a small section is readable despite damage.
{LINE_SPACE}
...It's almost time. The Tuatha will be begin their attack soon. It may all come down to this after so many years. Soon, I think, the war will be decided one way or the other.
{LINE_SPACE}
I can't believe it's been over twenty years since I've been home. I hope mother is well. I've found myself thinking about her more often these days. Maybe twenty year is long enough; maybe after one last great battle it'll be time for me to head....
{LINE_SPACE}
{LINE_CENTER} The readable portion of the journal ends abruptly and the only other useful information you can gleam is the constant mention of someplace called the Icebrine Coast.
